I do consider this suboptimal.  A Caveman cannot twoweapon in vanilla,
therefore the shield is its ideal source for reflection if available
(leaving the armor slot open for GDSM, and the cloak slot open for
displacement).

A Caveman also has something like 7 Int and 7 Wis to start with, meaning
that the collective Pw available to such a class is diddly/squat.  To
make this character into a caster, the raw effort required is far more
than "just ascending".

Spellcasting _is_ nice.  But let's not pretend that forcing a square peg
into a round hole is anything close to "optimal".

